  "articleBody": "Starting a home renovation is exciting, but it's easy to stumble into common mistakes if you're not careful. One of the biggest pitfalls is focusing solely on the price tag. While budget is super important, going with the cheapest bid without checking credentials can lead to headaches down the road. Always make sure to verify your contractor's license and insurance. This isn't just a formality; it protects you if something goes wrong. Another frequent mistake? Not checking references from projects similar to yours. You want to see that your contractor has successfully completed work like what you're envisioning. And please, get everything in writing! The scope of work, the timeline, the warranty, and how change orders will be handled—it all needs to be clearly documented in a contract. Don't leave anything to assumptions. Skipping details about permits and inspections is another big no-no; confirm who's responsible for those critical steps. By being thorough and proactive, you can avoid these common pitfalls and ensure your renovation project with a reputable company like HH Remodeling LLC, serving the Denver area, goes smoothly and turns out exactly as you hoped. A little extra effort upfront can save you a lot of stress and money later on.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
